            connect launchpad
            connect aeolus

Building on rpi is sloowwww. I tried to figure out how to cross-compile and
didn't find an easy way (one needs to be proficient in dark magic)

But this is the brilliant part about making a midi transport interface, because
I only have to build the linux stuff and iterating on that should only have to
rebuild the alsa file(s). I figured out that I should set updater.num_jobs=1 in
~/.tupoptions or the rpi runs out of RAM and starts thrashing. And building the
tests uses enough RAM that it gets swappy/takes forever to build, so just don't
do that.

Oh, bad news, spdlog blows up the ram and causes swapping. I guess it'll be
printf logging macros.
